":"visual","title":"Pear","creator":"Unknown","date":"","source":{"institution":"Kulturparken Småland via Europeana","work":null,"url":"https://www.europeana.eu/item/410/S_KPS_object_L113"},"rights":{"license":"CC-BY"},"editorial":{"note":"Large, almost clot-shaped pearl of glass flux. The decor is divided into square fields with red streaks in between. Every second field is chessy in yellow and black and every two is blue with a white flower.","noteSource":"source","room":"deep-time","tags":["photograph","europeana","design","object","pattern","archaeology","archaeology-ou-172","close-up","background","white-background","texture","shape","jewellery-ou-301","pear","new"],"tone":"sky","quality":1.231},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://mm.dimu.org/image/0334AwdyWXo5?dimension=1200x1200","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"80569":{"n":80569,"cl":907,"id":"eu-410_S_KPS_object_L815","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Tension","creator":"Unknown","date":"","source":{"institution":"Kulturparken Småland via Europeana","work":null,"url":"https://www.europeana.eu/item/410/S_KPS_object_L815"},"rights":{"license":"CC-BY"},"editorial":{"note":"Oval buckle of Cu alloy, consisting of two consecutive “shells.” The upper has broken decor with animal ornamentation and five buds, as well as two coarse layers of iron.","noteSource":"source","room":"deep-time","tags":["photograph","europeana","design","object","archaeology","archaeology-ou-172","artifact","texture","patina","ornate","fibula","tension","new"],"tone":"sky","quality":1.231},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://mm.dimu.org/image/0234AwdyWXo6?dimension=1200x1200","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"80570":{"n":80570,"cl":907,"id":"eu-410_S_KPS_object_L820","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Tension","creator":"Unknown","date":"","source":{"institution":"Kulturparken Småland via Europeana","work":null,"url":"https://www.europeana.eu/item/410/S_KPS_object_L820"},"rights":{"license":"CC-BY"},"editorial":{"note":"Oval buckle of gilded Cu alloy. Decor with braids and animal ornamentation and originally nine strapped buds (two missing). Underside with traces of the needle’s attachment and hook, as well as a storage associated with preservation (?).","noteSource":"source","room":"deep-time","tags":["photograph","europeana","sculpture","design","object","archaeology","archaeology-ou-172","carving","artifact","texture","fibula","tension","new"],"tone":"mauve","quality":1.231},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://mm.dimu.org/image/0234Awdx1XTe?dimension=1200x1200","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"80571":{"n":80571,"cl":907,"id":"eu-410_S_KPS_object_L821","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Tension","creator":"Unknown","date":"","source":{"institution":"Kulturparken Småland via Europeana","work":null,"url":"https://www.europeana.eu/item/410/S_KPS_object_L821"},"rights":{"license":"CC-BY"},"editorial":{"note":"Reflective buckle of Cu alloy. Ornamented in the form of the three norns (or three bears?) with the heads facing the central part of the span. On the back are remnants of the bracket and iron needle, as well as part of a suspension loop.","noteSource":"source","room":"deep-time","tags":["photograph","europeana","design","object","archaeology","archaeology-ou-172","artifact","texture","patina","ornate","fibula","tension","new"],"tone":"paper","quality":1.231},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://mm.dimu.org/image/0234AwdyWXo7?dimension=1200x1200","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"80572":{"n":80572,"cl":907,"id":"eu-410_S_KPS_object_L825","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Tension","creator":"Unknown","date":"","source":{"institution":"Kulturparken Småland via Europeana","work":null,"url":"https://www.europeana.eu/item/410/S_KPS_object_L825"},"rights":{"license":"CC-BY"},"editorial":{"note":"Round costume fibula of Cu alloy. Decor of winding, linear bands. Central is a square with a slight elevation. The outer edge smooth, but slightly succumbs to four opposite sides.","noteSource":"source","room":"deep-time","tags":["photograph","europeana","object","pattern","archaeology","archaeology-ou-172","close-up","artifact","texture","shape","patina","fibula","tension","new"],"tone":"mauve","quality":1.231},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://mm.dimu.org/image/0234Awdx1Cfa?dimension=1200x1200","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"80575":{"n":80575,"cl":907,"id":"eu-410_S_KPS_object_M1478","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Tutulus","creator":"Unknown","date":"","source":{"institution":"Kulturparken Småland via Europeana","work":null,"url":"https://www.europeana.eu/item/410/S_KPS_object_M1478"},"rights":{"license":"CC-BY"},"editorial":{"note":"Tutulus av brons. Toppen avbruten och stora delar av kanten bortbruten. Täta koncentriska cirklar upp mot toppen. Avbrutet fäste i form av en bronstorne på undersidan. Troligen bronsålderns persod II-III.","noteSource":"source","room":"deep-time","tags":["photograph","europeana","object","archaeology","archaeology-ou-172","background","texture","rough-texture","jewellery-ou-301","tutulus","new"],"tone":"sky","quality":1.231},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://mm.dimu.org/image/0334ASys33tm?dimension=1200x1200","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"80608":{"n":80608,"cl":907,"id":"eu-410_S_KPS_object_M17000_1960","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Prydnadsbleck","creator":"Unknown","date":"","source":{"institution":"Kulturparken Småland via Europeana","work":null,"url":"https://www.europeana.eu/item/410/S_KPS_object_M17000_1960"},"rights":{"license":"CC-BY"},"editorial":{"note":"Triangulärt prydnadsbleck av silver som dock är avbrutet längs ena sidan. Från mitten och nedåt är små drivna bucklor, varav den största har en mittknopp. Utifrån bucklorna går graverade raka och vågiga linjer.","noteSource":"source","room":"deep-time","tags":["photograph","europeana","pattern","archaeology","archaeology-ou-172","macro-photography","close-up","background","white-background","texture","shape","jewellery-ou-301","blade-pendant","ornamental-plaque","new"],"tone":"mauve","quality":1.231},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://mm.dimu.org/image/0331yxsnJ5hX?dimension=1200x1200","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"80610":{"n":80610,"cl":907,"id":"eu-410_S_KPS_object_M17000_1964","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Medallion","creator":"Unknown","date":"","source":{"institution":"Kulturparken Småland via Europeana","work":null,"url":"https://www.europeana.eu/item/410/S_KPS_object_M17000_1964"},"rights":{"license":"CC-BY"},"editorial":{"note":"Fragments of some oval medallion of blank polished jet, or pitch carbon and gagate as it is also called. The badge is now in two parts and about 1/4 of the medallion is completely missing.","noteSource":"source","room":"deep-time","tags":["photograph","europeana","art","object","archaeology","archaeology-ou-172","figure","medallion","artifact","texture","shape","man","jewellery-ou-301","new"],"tone":"mauve","quality":1.231},"media":{"kind":"image","url":"https://mm.dimu.org/image/0231uUNSyC7S?dimension=1200x1200","fallback":null,"poster":null,"start":null,"end":null,"duration":null}},"80621":{"n":80621,"cl":907,"id":"eu-410_S_KPS_object_M17000_2005","type":"image","cat":"visual","title":"Metallföremål","creator":"Unknown","date":"","source":{"institution":"Kulturparken Småland via Europeana","work":null,"url":"https://www.europeana.eu/item/410/S_KPS_object_M17000_2005"},"rights":{"license":"CC-BY"},"editorial":{"note":"Oregelbundet klippt plåt med en rak kant. Hoprullad och hopklämd. Vid kanten en grupp spikhål.","noteSource":"source","room":"deep-time","tags":["photograph","europeana","modern-art","copper","object","archaeology","archaeology-ou-172","close-up","p